  "synthesis": "# Second-Pass Audit Synthesis — Callisto Workspace\n\n**Scope:** 29 verified findings (4 high / 14 medium / 11 low) across duplication, performance, and architecture, audited at `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a4d9da1eb071e1590` (branch `refactor/manifest-reader-and-parallel-arms`).\n\n**Verdict on the prior refactor round:** clean but incomplete. I git-blamed every finding's primary lines. **Zero findings were introduced as regressions by the 9-PR round** (`22ccf181`…`f22864e7`). But **9 findings live in files the round edited and left untouched**, and **2 are asymmetries the round itself created or knowingly walked past** — `F2` (the round fixed the Linked-group guard in `#59` and left the identical Fixed-group hole four lines below) and `F26` (the round created `set_scalar_preserving_decor` in `cargo.rs` while editing `python.rs` in the same round, leaving python's hand-rolled twin). The round fixed *instances*; it did not install the *owner* that stops recurrence. Every pattern below is a missing owner.\n\n---\n\n## Part 1 — Patterns\n\n### Pattern A — Parallel arms maintained only by convention\n**Root cause:** N structurally-identical code arms (two branches, two ecosystems, two modes, four methods) with no single owner. A correctness fix lands on one arm; the compiler cannot force the others. This is literally the failure mode \"audit pattern H\" targeted — the round unified four such pairs and stopped.\n\n| ID | Instance | Sev |\n|---|---|---|\n| F2 | `cascade.rs:370-398` Fixed-group convergence lacks the stale-member guard its Linked sibling got in `08814168` → panic at `commands/version.rs:147` | high |\n| F17 | `identity.rs:38-78` `PackageId::parse` repeats empty/leading-hyphen/traversal checks in both the `:` and `/` branches (duplication *freshly created* by `f66aae88`) | med |\n| F14 | `bump.rs` SemVer (74-153) vs PEP 440 (184-266) bump arithmetic typed out twice; history shows the same bug fixed independently on each copy (`99a632e3`, `5c86c315`) | med |\n| F18 | `is_safe_github_repository` (release.rs:1049) vs `valid_repo_part` (release_pr.rs:406) — same concept, **divergent rules** | med |\n| F11 | `cli/commands/snapshot.rs:17-34` ≡ `cli/commands/tag.rs:15-32` strict-escalation block, both hardcoding `escalate(.., true, true)` | med |\n| F12 | `vcs/access.rs:119-155` native-then-shell fallback written four times (`head_sha`, `list_tags`, `resolve_commit`, `commits_since`) | med |\n| F19 | `graph/commands/tag.rs:95-107` ≡ `119-129` already-existed/resolve-target logic across preview and write branches | low |\n\n**Fixes**\n\n- **F2 (do first, ~15 lines):** mirror the Linked block verbatim — build `live_members` by filtering on `input.base.contains_key(id)`, push the same `DiagnosticCode::UnknownPackage` warning with `ConfigKey::FIXED_GROUP`, and iterate `live_members` in both the severity-raise loop and the target-insert loop. Confirmed necessary: `groups::fixed_group_target` (groups.rs:81-104) silently tolerates a stale member (`unwrap_or_else(|| Version::semver(1,0,0))`) rather than erroring, so the stale id really does reach `out.targets` and then `pkg_map.get(id).copied().unwrap()`.\n- **F17:** extract `fn validate_prefixed_remainder(prefix: &str, remainder: &str, s: &str) -> Result<(), PackageIdParseError>`; call from both branches.\n- **F14:** extract `fn bump_release_triple(major, minor, patch, sev, finalize_in_place) -> Result<(u64,u64,u64), BumpError>` used by both `bump()` impls, plus a shared \"find trailing numeric counter after prefix, increment\" helper for both `bump_prerelease()` impls. ~60 lines → one algorithm, one test matrix.\n- **F18:** pick the strict rule (`valid_repo_part`), move it to one crate-internal `fn validate_github_repository(&str)`, and have `GitHubAttestationPolicyV1::new` adopt it — see triage note T5, this is a behavior tightening on persisted data.\n- **F11:** add `fn abort_on_crosscheck_failures(ws: &Workspace, strict_graph: bool) -> Result<(), CliError>` in `cli/commands/mod.rs`; also fix the hardcoded `true, true` to honor the actual flag (status/validate/version already do).\n- **F12:** one generic `fn read_with_fallback<T>(&self, native: impl FnOnce(&GitRepository) -> Result<T, VcsError>, shell: impl FnOnce() -> Result<T, VcsError>) -> Result<T, VcsError>`. **Caveat:** keep it private/read-only — writes (`create_tag`, access.rs:156-170) deliberately do *not* fall back, and a reusable public helper would erode that distinction.\n- **F19:** extract `fn resolve_existing_or_release_sha(...)` alongside the already-extracted `plan_floating_major` — the file has the precedent.\n\n---\n\n### Pattern B — Canonical helper exists; call sites were never migrated\n**Root cause:** a helper was added specifically to close a gap, but adoption was never enforced (no lint, no deletion of the old path). Half the \"fix\" is still shipped.\n\n| ID | Instance | Sev |\n|---|---|---|\n| F3 | `tags.rs:136-137` builds the default tag template via `TagTemplate::parse(&format!(\"{}@{{version}}\", …))` instead of `TagTemplate::default_for` — and the two paths **behave differently** (`parse` validates git-ref legality, `default_for` does not) | high |\n| F10 | `cli/commands/publish.rs:16-20` and `cli/render/mod.rs:54-70` each re-derive plan emptiness by hand; `PublishPlan::is_empty()` (plan.rs:49) exists *and its test comment names this exact duplicate* | med |\n| F15 | `callisto-moon/src/runner.rs:32` throws away a real `io::Error` and string-matches `\"not found\"`; sibling `cli/runner.rs:43-49` does it correctly via `e.kind() == ErrorKind::NotFound` | med |\n| F21 | `pr_body.rs:159` does an O(bumps × changelog_writes) `.find()` in a loop; sibling `plan_version` fixed exactly this twice (PERF-006/008 `HashMap`) | low |\n| F25 | `CargoToml::publish_targets` (cargo.rs:242-248) is a byte-equivalent dead shadow of the `Manifest` trait default (lib.rs:91-103) | low |\n\n**Fixes**\n\n- **F3:** replace with `TagTemplate::default_for(&pkg.id)` in `TagIndex::build`. Decide the validation question explicitly: either `default_for` gains the ref-name check (and returns `Result`), or the check is documented as intentionally absent. Today the same package name is accepted by `release.rs` and rejected by `tags.rs`.\n- **F10:** `if plan.is_empty()` at both sites; in `render_publish` keep `total_packages` for display but branch on `is_empty()`.\n- **F15:** classify from `e.kind()` on the native path before `.to_string()`; keep `looks_like_not_found` for `runner_pdk.rs` only (warpgate errors genuinely carry no `ErrorKind`). Note the existing test `native_runner_reports_not_found` passes only by accident of the platform's ENOENT wording.\n- **F21:** build `HashMap<&PackageId, &ChangelogWrite>` once before the loop.\n- **F25:** delete the override (`CargoToml::ecosystem()` returns `Cargo`, so the default dispatches identically).\n\n---\n\n### Pattern C — `callisto-manifests` exposes primitives but no composition or format-fidelity layer\n**Root cause:** `common.rs` was created for parsing primitives only. Anything else cross-cutting — line-ending fidelity, context construction, mutate/persist lifecycle — stayed private per module or got improvised by callers, so it was applied inconsistently.\n\n| ID | Instance | Sev |\n|---|---|---|\n| F4 | `CargoToml` tracks only `has_bom`; npm and python each independently invented an identical private `enum LineEnding` + detect/reapply. **Cargo.toml has no CRLF preservation at all** — a live violation of CLAUDE.md's named \"Format Preservation\" invariant, with no CRLF fixture or test for Cargo anywhere | high |\n| F26 | `python.rs:311-322` `set_with_decor` reinvents `cargo.rs:120-131` `set_scalar_preserving_decor` — the helper the round *just created* | low |\n| F9 | The ~15-line \"load workspace cargo inheritance + detect npm workspace kind + build `OpenContext`\" block is copy-pasted at `walk.rs:81`, `lib.rs:166`, `apply.rs:110`, `commands/version.rs:279`; no shared constructor exists anywhere (grep of `OpenContext {` finds only these four plus test literals) | med |\n| F13 | `WorkspaceCargoResolver::write_version`/`write_dependency` each call `self.persist()` internally, breaking the mutate/persist split every other `Manifest` impl honors; `apply_version_plan` therefore excludes root-routed writes from batching and rewrites the *same* root `Cargo.toml` N+1 times per run | med |\n\n**Fixes**\n\n- **F4:** add `pub(crate) struct FormatFingerprint { has_bom: bool, line_ending: LineEnding }` in `common.rs` with `detect(&str)` / `apply(String) -> String`. Migrate npm and python onto it (pure refactor, existing CRLF tests are the safety net), then add it to `CargoToml::open`/`persist`. Add a CRLF `Cargo.toml` to `callisto_fixtures::corpus` — its absence is why this never surfaced.\n- **F26:** lift the decor-preserving write into `common.rs` (generic over `Table::insert` vs `Item` indexing, or two thin wrappers over one core) and delete both local copies. No ecosystem semantics live in either copy.\n- **F9:** add `impl OpenContext { pub fn for_workspace_root(root: &Path) -> Self }` in `callisto-manifests`; replace all four sites. Bonus: kills four redundant root-`Cargo.toml` reads per command run.\n- **F13:** split `WorkspaceCargoResolver` into mutate-only methods + an explicit `persist(permit)`, then let `classify_manifest_writes` route root-manifest writes into `batched` keyed on the root path. Sequence this **after** F9. See triage note T6 — `ApplyPermit` accounting must stay exact.\n\n---\n\n### Pattern D — Redundant reads outside the one cache that exists\n**Root cause:** `manifest_cache.rs` was introduced to make each manifest path read once per command — but only along `ManifestWalkResolver`'s open path. Identity resolution, npm role detection, group-owner lookups, and git blob reads each re-read from scratch. Costs scale with fan-in and package count, not with work done.\n\n| ID | Instance | Cost shape | Sev |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F8 | `commands/version.rs:296-335` re-opens+re-parses the **owner's** manifest once per platform target | O(targets) per owner, every `callisto version` | med |\n| F16 | `MoonProjectLocator::declared_edges` re-resolves `from` per project and `to` **per dependency edge**; `IdentityResolver::resolve` does a fresh `read_to_string` + parse with zero memoization and bypasses `manifest_cache` entirely | O(fan-in) — a 30-dependent utils crate is parsed 30+ times per load | med |\n| F23 | `detect_npm_role` does a raw `fs::read` + `serde_json` on every `package.json` *before* `open_cached` reads the same file again (the function's own doc comment admits this) | 2× I/O per npm package | low |\n| F20 | `derive_release_commit_decision` spawns 2 `git show` subprocesses per canonical manifest to verify one release commit | 2N process spawns | low |\n\n**Fixes**\n\n- **F8:** hoist `open(&owner_manifest_decl, &open_ctx)?` above the `group.members(PlatformManifest)` loop (or route it through `manifest_cache::open_cached`). Owner deps do not change across platform iterations. Smallest fix in this pattern.\n- **F16:** give `IdentityResolver` a `BTreeMap<(PathBuf, Ecosystem), PackageId>` memo, or have `declared_edges` accept the already-resolved map from `projects()`. Both callers are in `walk.rs:79/535`, one call site each.\n- **F23:** the doc comment names the real fix — add `fn npm_role(&self) -> Option<NpmRole>` to `Manifest` (default `None`) and read it off the cached `PackageJson`.\n- **F20:** replace the per-manifest `git show` pair with two `git cat-file --batch` invocations (one per commit). Only two commits are ever queried. Defer unless release verification latency is actually observed.\n\n---\n\n### Pattern E — Release-domain derivation duplicated across the trust boundary it guards\n**Root cause:** `release_decision.rs`'s own module doc warns that duplicated derivation \"drifts\" — for a *different* function. The rule wasn't applied to its neighbors.\n\n| ID | Instance | Sev |\n|---|---|---|\n| F6 | package → `ReleasePackageId` per canonical manifest per ecosystem is rebuilt in `derive_release_decision` (22-30), `derive_release_commit_decision` (194-200 **and again** at 208-211 in the same function), and `release.rs:639-653` | med |\n| F7 | `PublishTarget` variant semantics (dispatchable? fingerprint contribution? registry override?) live in three independent matches: `release.rs:970-1003`, `release.rs:1013-1046`, `publish.rs:355-429` — while `ecosystem.rs:113-148` already offers a partial capability layer neither fingerprint site uses | med |\n\n**Fixes**\n\n- **F6:** one `fn release_package_ids(package: &Package) -> Result<Vec<ReleasePackageId>, GraphError>` in `release_decision.rs`; call from all three sites and delete the in-function recomputation at 208-211. This is the pair that produces and then *verifies* the same roster — drift here is a silent trust-boundary failure, which is why a medium-severity duplication earns a high priority slot.\n- **F7:** extend the existing `ecosystem.rs` capability layer rather than inventing a second one — add `fn registry_override(&self) -> Option<&str>` and `fn fingerprint_kind(&self) -> &'static str`, and switch `publish.rs`'s dispatchability check onto `Ecosystem::is_implemented()`. See triage note T4.\n\n---\n\n### Pattern F — Durable wire-type boilerplate with no abstraction\n**Root cause:** hand-written serde/newtype scaffolding replicated per type; each new durable type copies the last one.\n\n| ID | Instance | Sev |\n|---|---|---|\n| F27 | \"deserialize into private `Wire`, gate `schema_version`, forward to constructor\" hand-written 6× (`release.rs:293`, `release.rs:1195`, `release_pr.rs:60/121/275/602`) | low |\n| F28 | `GroupName`, `RegistryKey`, `TagName` — identical derive lists, `as_str`, `Display`; `CommitSha` is a fourth, inconsistently shaped | low |\n| F29 | `execute_extension` (`extension_pdk.rs:32-116`) rebuilds `ExecuteExtensionOutput { report: json_val.clone(), rendered: e.to_string(), exit_code: 1 }` five times; the `.clone()` is dead in every copy | low |\n\n**Fixes:** one `fn schema_gate(found: u8, expected: u8, type_name: &str) -> Result<(), D::Error>` (or a `versioned_wire!` macro) for F27; a `string_newtype!` macro — or explicitly document why `CommitSha` differs — for F28; `fn error_output(json_val: Value, e: &impl Display) -> ExecuteExtensionOutput` next to `build_extension_output` for F29. All three are mechanical, low-risk, and best done as one cleanup PR.\n\n---\n\n### Standalone findings\n\n**F1 — `changed_since_last_tag` marks every package changed (high, correctness).** `changed.rs:52` calls `git.commits_since(Some(&qualified), &[])` with an **empty pathspec**, so it walks every commit in the repo since that package's tag and returns `Ok(true)` on any hit. In an active monorepo that is always non-empty, so the path-scoped `git diff --quiet` below it (lines 59-67) is effectively dead code. Consequences: `status.changed_since_last_tag` is meaningless, and spec §6.3's empty-changeset escape hatch can never fire. Contradicts docs/01-spec.md §G.9.3, which specifies no `commits_since` short-circuit at all.\n\n**Fix — and a correction to the finding's proposed fix:** compute `let paths = package_paths(pkg)` *above* the call and pass it in, so the short-circuit is scoped identically to the diff. Then **keep the polarity as-is**: non-empty scoped result → `Ok(true)`; empty → **fall through to the `git diff --quiet` check**, do not skip it. The finding proposes using an empty scoped result to skip the diff; that would drop detection of uncommitted working-tree changes, which `git diff --quiet <tag> -- <paths>` currently catches. Scoping alone fixes the bug and keeps the optimization honest.\n\n**F5 — `ReleaseOperationId`'s hand-written `Ord` violates the `Ord`/`Eq` contract (medium, correctness).** `Ord` folds `ArtifactUpload` down to `platform|asset_name` (release.rs:829-830, 850-851), dropping `attestation_policy`, while `Eq`/`Hash` are derived over the full struct and `ArtifactSlotId`'s own `Ord` *does* include the policy. Two `Eq`-distinct operations compare `Equal`, so `validate_operations`'s `BTreeSet` (line 1381) reports a false `DuplicateOperation` and `ReleaseIntentV1::new` rejects a legitimate intent. **Fix:** derive `PartialOrd`/`Ord` on `ReleaseOperationRole` (all field types are already `Ord`) and delete the hand-built tuple, or at minimum add the three attestation fields to it. Deriving is the fix that stays correct when a role gains a field.\n\n**F22 — `IdentityIndex` has no reverse index (low, architecture).** `native_name`/`native_names` (identity.rs:397-414) linear-scan `self.native` on every call, and `native_name` is called per dependent-edge inside `solve_cascade`'s rewrite loop (cascade.rs:256) → effectively O(E·P). **Fix:** populate a `BTreeMap<PackageId, Vec<(Ecosystem, String)>>` in the same `walk.rs` loop that already fills `native`/`prefixed`.\n\n**F24 — Test-only revwalk counter is permanent public global state (low, architecture).** `REVWALK_VISIT_COUNT` + two `pub fn` accessors (`vcs/lib.rs:214-232`) are ungated (the crate has no `[features]` section at all) and the counter is bumped unconditionally in the production per-commit loop (line 407). **Fix:** add a `test-util` feature and gate the statics/accessors behind it, or instrument at the test's call site. See triage note T3 — the doc comment claims precedent.\n\n---\n\n## Part 2 — Priority ranking\n\nWeighted by severity × blast radius, refactor-round proximity, and fix cost (S ≤ 30 min, M ≤ half day, L ≥ 1 day).\n\n### P0 — This week\n| Rank | ID | Why | Cost | Origin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **F2** cascade Fixed-group guard | Panic on a config a user can trivially create; the round fixed the identical sibling and left this | S | `11603671` (2026-08-17); **gap left by round PR #59** |\n| 2 | **F1** unscoped `commits_since` | Silently defeats per-package change detection; two documented behaviors are dead today | S | Pre-existing since `1a8f983d` |\n| 3 | **F3** default tag template | Two paths disagree on validation, not just style; one-line fix | S | Pre-existing (`c2a138b6`) |\n| 4 | **F5** `ReleaseOperationId` `Ord` | Wrongly rejects valid release intents; deriving removes the class | S | `eeda4a2f` (#39, 5 days old) |\n\n### P1 — Next\n| Rank | ID | Why | Cost | Origin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 5 | **F4** Cargo CRLF | Violates a CLAUDE.md-named invariant; unblocks Windows/`autocrlf` users; also unifies two ad hoc copies | M | Pre-existing gap |\n| 6 | **F6** `ReleasePackageId` ×3 | Drift here desynchronizes the release trust boundary from its own verifier | S | `eeda4a2f`; **file edited by round `7c43012f`** |\n| 7 | **F9** `OpenContext` ×4 | Enables F13; removes 4 redundant root reads/run | S | Original `1a8f983d` |\n| 8 | **F26** decor helper | The round created the helper and left the twin — closing it finishes pattern H | S | **Asymmetry created by round `10e28541`** |\n| 9 | **F10** `PublishPlan::is_empty` | The method exists solely for this; two files still ignore it | S | `a079bcc5`; **file edited by round twice** |\n| 10 | **F8** owner-manifest reopen | One-line hoist, real per-run I/O win on napi workspaces | S | `431feb92` |\n| 11 | **F15** `ErrorKind` classification | Downgrades a type-checkable invariant to a locale-dependent heuristic | S | Original |\n\n### P2 — Scheduled cleanup (batch as 2-3 PRs)\n| Rank | IDs | Grouping | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 12 | **F17, F19, F11, F12** | Pattern A mechanical extractions — one PR, four helpers | M |\n| 13 | **F16, F23** | Identity/role read caching in the moon+walk path | M |\n| 14 | **F14** | SemVer/PEP 440 bump arithmetic unification; history proves the cost of leaving it | M |\n| 15 | **F18** | Repo-identity validator unification — **behavior change, needs triage T5** | M |\n| 16 | **F13** | Resolver mutate/persist split + root-manifest batching (after F9) | L |\n| 17 | **F25, F21