    refactor(format): extract shared bump-triple and counter-increment helpers

    SemVerVersioning::bump and Pep440Versioning::bump implemented the exact
    same major.minor.patch zero-guard bump algorithm, one on Version, the
    other on a raw (u64, u64, u64) triple. SemVerVersioning::bump_prerelease
    and Pep440Versioning::bump_prerelease duplicated the same pattern again:
    compute the finalized release, scan the current version's rendered
    string for a trailing tag+counter suffix, increment it, reassemble.

    This wasn't incidental convergence -- git history shows two independent
    bug-fix commits were needed for the same arithmetic on each copy
    (99a632e3 for the SemVer counter, 5c86c315 for the PEP 440 post+dev
    bump), meaning a correctness fix has to be rediscovered and reapplied
    per copy.

    Extract bump_release_triple (the zero-guard arithmetic, parameterized
    by finalize_in_place) and next_counter (parse-and-increment a trailing
    decimal suffix), used by both grammars' bump/bump_prerelease. Pure
    refactor -- all existing SemVer and PEP 440 test cases pass unchanged.

