commit 1141cf5f58c3d1c68081bb0fc3023b5208d3fa61
Author: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 15:30:16 2026 -0700

    perf(manifests,graph): batch WorkspaceCargoResolver writes into one persist per root manifest

    WorkspaceCargoResolver::write_version/write_dependency each called
    persist() internally, so apply_version_plan had to process every
    CargoWorkspacePackage/CargoWorkspaceDependency write individually --
    a monorepo release touching the workspace version plus several
    workspace-inherited dependencies read-parsed-and-wrote the same root
    Cargo.toml N+1 times in one apply_version_plan call.

    Split write_version/write_dependency into pure in-memory mutation and
    a separate, explicitly-called persist (mirroring CargoToml/PackageJson/
    PyprojectToml's existing split), and teach classify_manifest_writes to
    route root-manifest writes into a resolver_batched group when the same
    physical file has no competing Manifest-trait write -- the mixed-routing
    data-loss hazard classify_manifest_writes already guards against is
    untouched; those paths still get no batching on either side.

    New resolver_load_call_count/resolver_persist_call_count counters
    (kept separate from open_call_count/persist_call_count, since
    OpenContext::for_workspace_root loads the resolver unconditionally)
    prove the shared root manifest is now opened and persisted exactly
    once per apply_version_plan call, regardless of how many bumps/
    rewrites target it.

