{"type":"idle_notification","from":"adv-unwrap-017","timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:48:12.982Z","idleReason":"available","result":"**Verdict: REFUTED (stale code — the flagged lines no longer exist at HEAD).**\n\nThe function is `operation_id_text` at `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/release.rs:1437`. It contains zero `unwrap_or` calls; `grep -n 'unwrap_or' crates/callisto-model/src/release.rs` returns no matches for the entire file.\n\nThe excerpted code was deleted by commit `a32f8b67` (\"fix(graph,model): correctness batch — ... Ord/Eq violation (#64)\"), which `git merge-base --is-ancestor a32f8b67 HEAD` confirms is already in the current branch. The diff for that commit shows exactly the flagged lines being removed (`- .map(|registry| registry.registry_key().as_str()) - .unwrap_or(\"\")`, twice, plus the `.unwrap_or_default()`). The scanner was reading a pre-`a32f8b67` snapshot.\n\n**On the crux question the finding raised — the answer is \"security-relevant,\" so the concern was well-aimed, just aimed at code that's already fixed.** `operation_id_text` is *not* Display/logging. Its only two non-test callers are `digest_intent` (release.rs:1381 and :1383), which feeds each operation id and each prerequisite id into a `CanonicalTranscript` that is hashed by `IntentDigest::from_transcript`. That digest is the durable authorization commitment for a release intent. So under the old code, two `RegistryPublish` roles with different registry bindings could both have serialized as `publish::` and produced an identical intent digest.\n\n**Why the current code cannot reproduce that, structurally:**\n- `ReleaseOperationRole::RegistryPublish { registry: RegistryBindingId }` (release.rs:791) holds a non-`Option` field, so the `match` arm binds a value that always exists — there is nothing to `unwrap_or` on.\n- `RegistryBindingId::registry_key()` and `binding_digest()` (release.rs:771, :776) return `&RegistryKey` / `&RegistryBindingDigest`, not `Option`.\n- Empty is unrepresentable even at construction: `validated_registry_key` (release.rs:1246) rejects `raw.is_empty()` with `MalformedRegistryKey`, and both `RegistryBindingId::new` and the `Deserialize` impl (release.rs:748-756, :818-835) route through it, so a hostile serialized payload can't smuggle an empty key in either.\n- The `match` on `id.role` is exhaustive with no catch-all arm, so a future variant forces a compile error rather than silently degrading.\n\nAdjacent observation, not a confirmed finding and out of this candidate's scope: `operation_id_text` joins components with `|` and `:` into a *single* transcript field. `CanonicalTranscript::push_length_prefixed` (release.rs:631) length-prefixes each tag/value pair, so there is no cross-field ambiguity, but the intra-string separators are not themselves escaped. The component grammars (ASCII-alphanumeric-plus-`-_` registry keys, hex digests, rendered semver) appear to make a collision unconstructible today; I did not trace `slot.platform` / `slot.asset_name` grammars, which are the less-constrained inputs to that same format string."}
