commit c7d6a9538ec089308460b3509ca2cc789004e385
Author: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 16:44:01 2026 -0700

    fix(vcs,graph,cli): report accurate causes for lock, identity, and severity-validation errors

    Three error/diagnostic messages told the operator the wrong thing:

    - callisto-vcs: ReleaseWorkspaceLock::acquire blamed "another Callisto
      release already holds this workspace lock" for every lock-acquisition
      failure (permission denied, disk full, unsupported filesystem, etc.),
      not just genuine contention. Now distinguishes fs2::lock_contended_error's
      ErrorKind (true contention) from other I/O failures and reports the real
      cause for the latter.
    - callisto-graph: IdentityResolver::resolve collapsed both an
      unsupported-ecosystem case and a genuine PackageId parse failure into
      GraphError::AmbiguousName, which is wrong for both. Added
      UnsupportedIdentityEcosystem and PackageIdentifierParse variants so each
      failure reports its own accurate cause.
