me":"Parser rejection reasons discarded for user-supplied identifiers","count":3,"shape":".map_err(|_error| SomeError::Invalid{ raw }) discarding a multi-variant FromStr-style parse error (GitHubRepositoryParseError, PackageIdParseError) that already distinguishes the specific rejection reason, replacing it with a message that only restates the input string back at the user","representative_examples":[{"file":"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release_pr.rs","line":53,"discarded_cause":"GitHubRepositoryParseError::{MissingSeparator, TooManyParts, InvalidOwner, InvalidRepo} -- four textually distinct, differently-actionable parse failures","folded_into":"ReleasePrDecisionError::InvalidRepository { repository }","harm":"A user who typed `owner/repo/extra` (too many parts) gets the identical error as one who typed `owner#repo` (invalid characters) or `justonestring` (no separator) -- the message names only the bad string, not what specifically about it is wrong, even though the parser already knew."},{"file":"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs","line":574,"discarded_cause":"PackageId::ParseError distinguishing a syntactically malformed identifier (leading slash/hyphen, path traversal, bad ecosystem prefix) from a well-formed identifier","folded_into":"GraphError::UnknownPackage { id }","harm":"This conflates two operationally different situations under one label: 'you typed an invalid package identifier' (fix: correct your syntax) vs. 'you typed a valid identifier but no such package exists in this workspace' (fix: check the package list) -- these call for different next steps and the collapsed message can't tell the operator which one applies."}]},{"name":"Version/grammar comparison mismatch loses the actual grammar pair","count":2,"shape":"Version::compare(...).map_err(|_grammar_mismatch| ...) reconstructs a new error without the GrammarMismatch{left, right} payload that compare() already produced","representative_examples":[{"file":"crates/callisto-graph/s