med_sites":40,"systemic_fix_warranted":true,"systemic_fix_rationale":"The dominant category alone (28 of 40 confirmed sites) is a single crate collapsing dozens of textually and semantically distinct causes -- rich, purpose-built multi-variant enums (ArtifactManifestError, RegistryError with RateLimited/AuthFailed payloads), parse errors, and git-command failures -- into one bare unit variant (GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale) whose fixed help text is actively misleading for most of the real causes it now stands in for. That is not scattered carelessness; it is a load-bearing convention in callisto-graph's release path (the single most safety-critical code in the workspace, per its own doc comments about \"no release operation was authorized\"), and per-site patches would leave the next release-path bug hidden behind the same sink. The second and sixth categories (parser-rejection folding, and VcsError::Git(String) lacking any #[source] field) are structural too: PackageIdParseError and GitHubRepositoryParseError already do the work of distinguishing causes and it is thrown away at the one or two call sites that surface it to a human, and VcsError::Git's shape makes a real source chain impossible even for call sites that want one -- 65 of 67 constructions work around this by manually interpolating {e} into a String, which is itself evidence the type should carry a #[source] instead. A workspace-wide fix is warranted: (1) give GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale a `reason: ReleaseIntentStaleReason` field (or split it into a handful of #[source]-carrying variants) so the ~28 sites above compile only if they pass the real cause through; (2) add a #[source] field to VcsError::Git (or a `Git { message: String, #[source] source: Option<...> }` shape) so the crate's own {e}-interpolation convention becomes structural instead of a manual habit; (3) add a workspace clippy/CI check that flags `.map_err(|_` and bare unit-variant catch-alls in non-test code, since the existing 40 site