6	{"type":"result","key":"v2:e93c9bea4694db08eb62aa3086600e2ffd588a7544c9b0ea089b635c3c891777","agentId":"a075f1cbf0d1e025d","result":{"problem":"Callisto already denies error-cause erasure -- `map_err_ignore = \"deny\"` sits in `[workspace.lints.clippy]` (Cargo.toml:64) -- but clippy's lint only matches the bare `|_|` pattern. The workspace has 0 `.map_err(|_|` sites and 42 `.map_err(|_error|` / `|_err|` / `|_e|` / `|_parse_err|` sites across 16 files in 7 crates: the codebase converged on the one spelling that evades the guard rail it turned on. 24 of those sites plus 4 catch-all match arms feed one unit variant, `GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale` (crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:238, code E124, help \"Regenerate and reapprove the release intent; no release operation was authorized\"), which has ~100 construction sites in release.rs (55), release_decision.rs (44) and release_execution.rs (2). Because it is a unit variant, nothing forces a cause through it: release.rs:359 discards `RegistryError::RateLimited(Duration)` / `AuthFailed` from the registry-output classifiers that were written specifically to distinguish those; release_execution.rs:46 discards the 5-variant `ArtifactManifestError` even though `GraphError::ArtifactManifest { #[source] source: ArtifactManifestError }` (E136, error.rs:254-262) already exists for exactly that; release_decision.rs:139/146/195/329 discard `ModelError::InvalidCommitSha`, `serde_json::Error` and `VersionParseError`, and the ~15 fail-closed checks in `derive_release_commit_decision` (lines 138-273) are indistinguishable at the terminal. This class has been patched per-instance before: `RegistryPublishUnconfirmed` (E157) was carved out of the same sink with a regression test asserting `!matches!(.., ReleaseIntentStale)` (release.rs:1216-1239). The same shape recurs in sibling enums: `VcsError::Git(String)` (callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:20-22) has no `#[source]` slot, so release_lock.rs:44/50 drop the `io::Error` entirely; `LocateError::MoonUnavailable` (locate/mod.rs:49-50) folds spawn failure and non-zero exit together and says so in its own message (locator.rs:36-40); `ConfigError::InvalidChangelogPath`/`InvalidChangesetsDir` (resolve.rs:260/323), `LocateError::OutsideWorkspaceRoot` (ignore_walk.rs:126), `ReleasePrDecisionError::InvalidRepository` (cli/release_pr.rs:53), `GraphError::UnknownPackage` at publish.rs:574 and `GroupGrammarMismatch` at cascade.rs:340 each rebuild an error without the multi-variant parse error (`ModelError`, `GitHubRepositoryParseError`, `PackageIdParseError`, `GrammarMismatch`) that already named the reason. All of these upstream types derive `thiserror::Error`, so carrying them costs nothing.","why_it_matters":"The release path is the code whose own doc comments claim \"no release operation was authorized\". Today that claim is printed for failures where an operation WAS dispatched: an npm publish that hits a 30s rate limit, an invalid registry token, a `git push` of the tag that exits non-zero, or a `gh release create` failure all render as E124 with advice to regenerate and reapprove the intent -- which is wrong for every one of them and, because the durable state deliberately stays `Attempting` (release_execution.rs:20-24), sends the operator away from the reconciliation step that is the actual next action during a live release. An operator whose CI built the wrong artifact slot roster is told the intent is stale; the intent was fine. An operator debugging a rejected release commit cannot tell which of ~15 checks tripped. Outside the release path, a read-only CI filesystem blocking the release-state directory prints \"could not create release state directory\" with no `io::Error`, and a broken `moon.yml` prints \"moon CLI is unavailable\" while moon's own stderr -- the one line that would say what is wrong -- is discarded. Maintainers pay too: E157 and E136 show this sink has already been fixed at least twice by adding a sibling variant, and with a unit variant and an evadable lint, the next contributor following the file's dominant pattern (`.map_err(|_error| GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale)`) reintroduces the defect with code that looks idiomatic for this repo and passes `just lint`.","proposal":"Two structural boundaries, one spec, sequenced so the gate lands last. (1) Close the lint evasion workspace-wide. Add `.github/tests/verify-error-erasure-gate.sh` (same shape as the existing `verify-release-workflow-contract.sh`) that fails on any `map_err(\\s*|_[A-Za-z_]` under `crates/**/*.rs` and on any `allow(clippy::map_err_ignore`, wired into both `just lint` and the `Workflow Contracts` CI job, with a fixture self-test. This funnels every erasure to the bare `|_|` spelling that `map_err_ignore = \"deny\"` already rejects; the only surviving route is `#[expect(clippy::map_err_ignore, reason = \"...\")]`, which rustc removes for you (unfulfilled_lint_expectations under -D warnings) when the erasure goes away and which reviewers can grep. An unused named binding (`|e|` without use) already fails `-D warnings` via rustc's unused_variables. Net effect: a bind-and-discard `map_err` cannot pass `just lint` without a written reason. No dylint/nightly infrastructure. (2) Make the sink variants unable to hold nothing. `GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale` becomes `ReleaseIntentStale { reason: ReleaseIntentStaleReason }` -- same code E124, same help text, Display gains `: {reason}` -- where `ReleaseIntentStaleReason` is a thiserror enum with one variant per fail-closed check and, for every variant that stands in for an upstream `Err` (ArtifactManifestError, ModelError, serde_json::Error, VersionParseError, CommandError, ReleaseIntentError, ReleaseOperationError, RegistryBindingIdError, ReleaseInputSnapshotError), a required `#[source]` field of that exact type; there is no payload-free `Other`/`Unknown` variant. Failures that occur after an operation has been dispatched (registry classification incl. `RegistryError::RateLimited`/`AuthFailed`, pypi build exit, `git tag`/`git push` failure, `gh release create` failure, post-effect verification mismatch, npm probe inconclusive) move to a new `GraphError::ReleaseOperationFailed { operation: ReleaseOperationId, #[source] source: ReleaseOperationFailure }` (E158) whose help text says the durable state remains `Attempting` and directs to reconciliation, never to intent regeneration -- generalizing the E157 precedent. release_execution.rs:46 uses the existing `GraphError::ArtifactManifest`. Sibling enums get the slot they lack: `VcsError::Io { context: &'static str, #[source] source: std::io::Error }`; `LocateError::MoonUnavailable` is replaced by `MoonSpawn { #[source] source: CommandError }` and `MoonProjectGraphFailed { exit_code: Option<i32>, stderr: String }`; `ConfigError::InvalidChangelogPath`/`InvalidChangesetsDir` and `LocateError::OutsideWorkspaceRoot` gain `#[source] source: ModelError`; `ReleasePrDecisionError::InvalidRepository` gains `#[source] source: GitHubRepositoryParseError`; new `GraphError::InvalidPackageId { raw, #[source] source: PackageIdParseError }` (E159) separates malformed-identifier from unknown-package at publish.rs:574; `GroupGrammarMismatch` gains `#[source] source: GrammarMismatch`. The remaining ~10 `|_x|` sites (exec.rs:201-202, tag.rs:268, snapshot.rs:30, bump.rs:114, pre_cursor.rs:28, add.rs:230, release.rs:1057/1121/1195) each either gain a source or are rewritten to `|_|` under `#[expect(..., reason)]` -- the gate forces the decision to be recorded either way. Sequencing: PR-A sibling enums + their sites; PR-B GraphError restructure (~100 mechanical constructor edits, test `matches!` patterns become `{ .. }`); PR-C the gate (turns green only once A and B land). Immediate scoped patch worth doing now, independent of the rest: release_execution.rs:46 -> `GraphError::ArtifactManifest { source }` (one line, variant already exists). release.rs:359 should be the first task of PR-B rather than patched twice.","outcome":"After merge: `just lint` (and the Workflow Contracts CI job) fails on any `.map_err(|_ident| ...)` anywhere under crates/, on any `#[allow(clippy::map_err_ignore)]`, and -- via the existing deny plus rustc -- on any `.map_err(|_| ...)` or unused `|e|` that lacks `#[expect(clippy::map_err_ignore, reason = \"...\")]`; `rg 'map_err\\(\\s*\\|_[A-Za-z_]' crates/` returns 0 (today 42). `GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale` cannot be written without a `reason`, and a reason that stands for an upstream error cannot be written without that error value (compile_fail doctest + source-chain unit test). A live-release npm rate limit renders as E158 with \"Rate limited. Retry after 30s\" in the cause chain and reconciliation guidance, not E124 \"regenerate and reapprove\"; a wrong artifact slot roster renders as E136 naming `MismatchedSlotRoster`; each of the fail-closed checks in `derive_release_commit_decision` renders a distinct reason. `moon` not on PATH and a broken `moon.yml` render as different LocateError variants, the latter carrying moon's stderr; an unwritable release-state directory renders the `io::Error` kind. E124's code, help text and fail-closed semantics are unchanged; `format_graph_error_json`'s shape is unchanged.","estimated_blast_radius":"~25 source files across 7 crates plus CI: 1 new script (.github/tests/verify-error-erasure-gate.sh) + its fixture self-test, Justfile `lint` recipe, callisto-ci.yml Workflow Contracts step; callisto-graph/src/error.rs (ReleaseIntentStale -> struct variant, new ReleaseIntentStaleReason + ReleaseOperationFailure enums, E158/E159 variants), commands/release.rs (55 constructor sites + tests), commands/release_decision.rs (44 sites + tests), commands/release_execution.rs (2), commands/publish.rs (1), cascade.rs (1), config/resolve.rs (2 + ConfigError fields), locate/mod.rs + locate/ignore_walk.rs (LocateError split/fields), callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs + release_lock.rs (new Io variant, 2 sites), callisto-moon/src/locator.rs + extension.rs test, callisto-cli release_pr.rs + add.rs, callisto-model exec.rs/tag.rs, callisto-format bump.rs, callisto-conventional pre_cursor.rs; ~100 mechanical ReleaseIntentStale edits are the bulk, the rest are 1-3 lines each. Three sequenced PRs (siblings; graph restructure; gate).","spec":{"id":"SPEC-ARCH-001","purpose":"Eliminate the error-cause-erasure class: error variants whose shape can be constructed with no upstream cause (unit variants, String-only wrappers) combined with a map_err spelling (`|_ident|`) that evades the workspace's existing `map_err_ignore = deny`, so that rich upstream errors (ArtifactManifestError, RegistryError, PackageIdParseError, GitHubRepositoryParseError, GrammarMismatch, ModelError, serde_json::Error, io::Error, CommandError) are silently replaced by a fixed, often-wrong message. The structural change makes cause-erasure fail `just lint` unless explicitly justified with `#[expect(clippy::map_err_ignore, reason)]`, and makes the release path's sink variant impossible to construct without a typed reason that carries its upstream source.","scope":"Two boundaries. (A) Workspace lint boundary: a CI/`just lint` gate script `.github/tests/verify-error-erasure-gate.sh` that rejects the `map_err(|_ident|` evasion spelling and any `allow(clippy::map_err_ignore`, leaving `#[expect(clippy::map_err_ignore, reason = \"...\")]` on a bare `|_|` closure as the sole escape hatch; applies to every `.rs` under `crates/`. (B) Error-type boundary: `callisto_graph::GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale` becomes a struct variant with a required `reason: ReleaseIntentStaleReason` (new thiserror enum; source-bearing variants carry `#[source]` of the exact upstream type; no payload-free catch-all); post-dispatch failures move to new `GraphError::ReleaseOperationFailed { operation, #[source] source: ReleaseOperationFailure }` (E158); sibling enums gain the slot they lack: `VcsError::Io { context, #[source] source: io::Error }`, `LocateError::MoonSpawn { #[source] source: CommandError }` + `LocateError::MoonProjectGraphFailed { exit_code, stderr }` replacing `MoonUnavailable`, `#[source] source: ModelError` on `ConfigError::InvalidChangelogPath`/`InvalidChangesetsDir`/`LocateError::OutsideWorkspaceRoot`, `#[source] source: GitHubRepositoryParseError` on `ReleasePrDecisionError::InvalidRepository`, new `GraphError::InvalidPackageId { raw, #[source] source: PackageIdParseError }` (E159), `#[source] source: GrammarMismatch` on `GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch`. Every existing `|_ident|` map_err site in crates/ is migrated in the same change set (gate is green on merge).","non_goals":["Restructuring `VcsError::Git(String)` itself or migrating its ~65 `format!(\"...: {e}\")` construction sites to a source chain -- their Display already preserves the cause; only io::Error sites move to the new `Io` variant.","Changing the validation logic or fail-closed semantics of any site that returns E124 today -- every such site still rejects; only its reason labeling changes.","Per-reason miette diagnostic codes -- E124 stays the single code for stale intent; the reason lives in Display and the source chain. Only E158 (ReleaseOperationFailed) and E159 (InvalidPackageId) are new codes.","A dylint/custom-clippy lint or nightly toolchain; the gate is a bash+rg contract script like the repo's existing `.github/tests/*.sh`.","Enabling `clippy::allow_attributes_without_reason` workspace-wide (17 unrelated `#[allow]` sites exist); only `allow(clippy::map_err_ignore` is rejected, by the gate.","Gating other discard shapes (`Err(_) =>` match arms, `unwrap_or_else(|_e|`, `.ok()`) -- for GraphError these are closed by the required-reason field; elsewhere they remain reviewer territory.","Changing the `--format json` / `format_graph_error_json` error envelope beyond message text.","Per-instance patching of the 40 sites as a standalone deliverable -- the only standalone patch recommended is release_execution.rs:46 -> existing `GraphError::ArtifactManifest`."],"acceptance_criteria":[{"id":"AC-001","criterion":"`.github/tests/verify-error-erasure-gate.sh` exits non-zero when any file under `crates/` matches the regex `map_err\\(\\s*\\|_[A-Za-z_]` or contains `allow(clippy::map_err_ignore`, and exits zero otherwise. Its fixture self-test (`.github/tests/test_error_erasure_gate.sh`) runs the script against three temp trees -- one with `.map_err(|_error| X)`, one with `#[allow(clippy::map_err_ignore)]`, one with `.map_err(|error| X { source: error })` plus `#[expect(clippy::map_err_ignore, reason = \"r\")] .map_err(|_| Y)` -- and asserts exit codes 1, 1, 0 respectively.","is_error_case":true},{"id":"AC-002","criterion":"The gate is invoked by the `lint` recipe in `Justfile` and by a step in the `Workflow Contracts` job of `.github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml`. Falsified by inserting `.map_err(|_e| GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale { .. })` into any crate and observing `just lint` exit zero.","is_error_case":false},{"id":"AC-003","criterion":"On the merged tree `rg -n 'map_err\\(\\s*\\|_[A-Za-z_]' crates/` returns zero matches (baseline today: 42), and `map_err_ignore = \"deny\"` remains in `[workspace.lints.clippy]` in the root Cargo.toml (test: `rg -q 'map_err_ignore = \"deny\"' Cargo.toml` in the gate script).","is_error_case":false},{"id":"AC-004","criterion":"Every remaining cause-discarding `map_err` in crates/ is spelled `.map_err(|_| ...)` under `#[expect(clippy::map_err_ignore, reason = \"...\")]`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` fails both when the attribute is absent (map_err_ignore) and when the attribute is present but the closure no longer discards (rustc unfulfilled_lint_expectations). Verified by a compile_fail doctest in callisto-graph containing an un-attributed `.map_err(|_| GraphError::UnsafeGitRemote { reason: \"x\" })`.","is_error_case":true},{"id":"AC-005","criterion":"`GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale` is a struct variant `ReleaseIntentStale { reason: ReleaseIntentStaleReason }` with diagnostic code E124 and help text unchanged from today, whose Display is `release intent no longer matches the current workspace snapshot: {reason}`. A `compile_fail` doctest on the variant containing `let _ = callisto_graph::GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale;` fails to compile (doctests run under `cargo test --doc --all-features` in `just test-ci`).","is_error_case":false},{"id":"AC-006","criterion":"`ReleaseIntentStaleReason` has no variant named `Other`, `Unknown`, `Generic`, or `Unspecified`, and every variant that is constructed from an upstream `Result::Err` stores it in a `#[source]` field of the exact upstream type (at minimum: ArtifactManifestError is NOT one of them -- see AC-008 -- but ModelError from CommitSha::parse, serde_json::Error, VersionParseError, CommandError, ReleaseIntentError, ReleaseOperationError, RegistryBindingIdError, ReleaseInputSnapshotError are). Unit test `release_intent_stale_reasons_expose_upstream_source` constructs one `GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale` per source-bearing variant and asserts that walking `std::error::Error::source` reaches a value that `downcast_ref`s to the upstream type. A variant storing `message: String` instead fails this test.","is_error_case":false},{"id":"AC-007","criterion":"Failures observed after an operation is dispatched -- registry CLI output classification (`classify_cargo_output`/`classify_npm_publish_output`/`classify_twine_output` returning Err), pypi build non-zero exit, `GitAccess::create_tag` Err, `git push` non-zero exit, `gh release create` failure, post-effect tag/forge verification mismatch, and an inconclusive `npm view` probe -- return `GraphError::ReleaseOperationFailed { operation: ReleaseOperationId, #[source] source: ReleaseOperationFailure }` with code E158 and help text stating the durable state remains `Attempting` and directing to reconciliation, and never `ReleaseIntentStale`. Test: `dispatch_registry` for an npm operation with a scripted runner whose publish output triggers `RegistryError::RateLimited(Duration::from_secs(30))` returns an error whose source chain contains exactly `RegistryError::RateLimited(Duration::from_secs(30))`, whose Display does not contain \"no release operation was authorized\", and for which `matches!(err, GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale { .. })` is false.","is_error_case":true},{"id":"AC-008","criterion":"`execute_release_with_artifacts` with a manifest whose `validate_for_intent` returns `Err(e)` returns `GraphError::ArtifactManifest { source: e }` (existing E136). Tests for at least `ArtifactManifestError::MismatchedSlotRoster` and `MismatchedAttestation` assert the exact source variant and `!matches!(err, GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale { .. })`; the `(false, None)` no-manifest arm returns `ReleaseIntentStale { reason: ReleaseIntentStaleReason::ArtifactManifestRequired }`.","is_error_case":true},{"id":"AC-009","criterion":"Each fail-closed check in `derive_release_commit_decision` yields a distinct `ReleaseIntentStaleReason` variant. Tests cover at least: HEAD != release commit (`HeadMismatch { expected, observed }`), decision file not added/modified in the commit (`DecisionNotFreshlyWritten { path }`), no changeset deleted (`NoChangesetConsumed`), malformed committed decision JSON (`DecisionUnparseable { path, #[source] source: serde_json::Error }`), claimed package's changelog untouched (`ChangelogNotUpdated { package }`), version changed for a package the decision never claimed (`UnclaimedVersionChange { package }`), claimed target version not observed (`ClaimedVersionNotApplied { package, expected, observed }`); each test asserts the specific variant so that no two checks can share one.","is_error_case":true},{"id":"AC-010","criterion":"`VcsError::Io { context: &'static str, #[source] source: std::io::Error }` exists with its own diagnostic code, and `ReleaseWorkspaceLock::acquire` against a parent directory that cannot be created returns it. Unix-only test (skipped when running as root): a 0o500 parent yields `VcsError::Io` whose `source.kind() == io::ErrorKind::PermissionDenied` and whose Display contains \"release state directory\". `rg 'map_err\\(\\|_' crates/callisto-vcs/src` returns zero matches.","is_error_case":true},{"id":"AC-011","criterion":"`LocateError::MoonUnavailable` no longer exists (compile-time: `rg 'MoonUnavailable' crates/` returns zero). `MoonProjectLocator::load_graph` returns `LocateError::MoonSpawn { source }` when `CommandRunner::run` returns `Err(CommandError::NotFound { program: \"moon\" })` (test asserts the source downcasts to that variant) and `LocateError::MoonProjectGraphFailed { exit_code: Some(1), stderr }` when the runner returns exit 1 with stderr `moon.yml: unknown field` (test asserts `err.to_string()` contains \"unknown field\"). `format_graph_error_json_has_stable_error_shape` in callisto-moon still passes with `code == \"E_GRAPH\"` and a non-empty message.","is_error_case":true},{"id":"AC-012","criterion":"Parser rejection reasons survive to the surfaced error: `ReleasePrDecisionError::InvalidRepository { repository, #[source] source: GitHubRepositoryParseError }` (test: `owner/repo/extra` -> source is `TooManyParts`; `owner#repo` -> `InvalidRepo` or `InvalidOwner`, distinct from `justonestring` -> `MissingSeparator`); `GraphError::InvalidPackageId { raw, #[source] source: PackageIdParseError }` (E159) is returned for `--package /leading` with source `LeadingSlash`, while `--package nonexistent` still returns `GraphError::UnknownPackage`; `ConfigError::InvalidChangelogPath`/`InvalidChangesetsDir` and `LocateError::OutsideWorkspaceRoot` carry `#[source] source: ModelError` (test: absolute changelog path -> source is `ModelError::AbsolutePath`); `GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch` carries `#[source] source: GrammarMismatch` (test: cascade group with SemVer and Pep440 members -> source `{ left: SemVer, right: Pep440 }`).","is_error_case":true},{"id":"AC-013","criterion":"The cause reaches the terminal: rendering `GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale { reason: DecisionUnparseable { .. } }` through the CLI's miette error path (the same `Report` rendering `callisto` uses for stderr) produces output containing both the E124 help text and serde_json's own message text (e.g. \"expected\"); rendering `ReleaseOperationFailed` from AC-007 produces output containing \"Retry after\" and not \"reapprove\". Falsified by any reason variant whose Display omits its source and whose `#[source]` is absent.","is_error_case":false},{"id":"AC-014","criterion":"Existing behaviour is preserved: every test that today asserts `Err(GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale)` passes with the pattern `Err(GraphError::ReleaseIntentStale { .. })`; the E157 regression test `require_registry_confirmation_rejects_unconfirmed_publish_with_its_own_variant` is unchanged and passing; `just ci-fast` is green with the gate wired in.","is_error_case":false}]}}}

